  {
   "id": "8UtQVsOhBwAJ",
   "from": "georg kessler",
   "author": "96fb6cad0e36014a",
   "date": "2018-04-10T07:28:57Z",
   "subject": "Re: jointly and freely estimating in multiple groups that can overlap",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello Drew and Terrence,<div><br></div><div>I came across a similar issue and a friend found me a solution. </div><div><br></div><div>The problem was the following: I had a MGM with 4 groups and a latent variable with three indicators. I wanted the loadings of one factor to be equal in group 2 and 3, but estimated freely in groups 1 and 4. The group.partial() command covers only releasing the parameter in all groups. Thus, I had a look at the tutorial. But this specific issue seems not to be covered there. Neither did I find any reference among the other resources offered on the lavaan-page.</div><div><br></div><div>With labeling I get equality constraints (check): </div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#606\">Deter</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">m1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">m1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">m1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">m1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rskminor</span></div></code></div></div></code></div><div><br></div>Coming from an Mplus-background I was thinking in defaults and thus wanting to override it with &quot;NA&quot;. To quote from the tutorial: &quot;multiply it with NA, as a hint to lavaan that the value of this parameter is still unknown&quot;. That&#39;s what I thought the solution ought to be:</div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Deter</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=~</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> c</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span><font color=\"#000000\">NA</font></span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">m1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">m1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span><font color=\"#000000\">NA</font></span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)*</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">rskminor</span><br></div></code></div><div>But that doesn&#39;t work. </div><div><br></div>The final solution was to assign a specific label to each parameter I want to estimate</div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Deter</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=~</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> c</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">m2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">m1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">m1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">m3</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)*</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">rskminor</span><br></div></code></div><br><br>Maybe an equal example could be added to the tutorial? </div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Georg</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br><br>On Friday, 17 February 2017 17:37:39 UTC+1, Drew Altschul  wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Took me a bit of finagling, but I got it to work the way I wanted after not too long. Thanks for the help!<br><br><br>On Tuesday, February 14, 2017 at 7:56:03 PM UTC, Terrence Jorgensen wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I *think* this should at very least be doable by specifying everything within the definition of the models<br></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>Indeed, you can see how to specify constraints on this page of the tutorial:</div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/syntax2.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/syntax2.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792425761855000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3P192qSvyLD8cLjDzaQ9dm\">http://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/syntax2.html</a><br></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Postdoctoral Researcher, Methods and Statistics</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">UvA web page: <a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792425761855000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1zcI65HDiMfUua39EorCwu\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div><div><br></div></div></div></div></blockquote></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "8CEasQvbAgAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2018-04-12T11:30:44Z",
   "subject": "Re: jointly and freely estimating in multiple groups that can overlap",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Coming from an Mplus-background I was thinking in defaults and thus wanting to override it with &quot;NA&quot;. To quote from the tutorial: &quot;multiply it with NA, as a hint to lavaan that the value of this parameter is still unknown&quot;. That&#39;s what I thought the solution ought to be:</div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Deter</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=~</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> c</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span><font color=\"#000000\">NA</font></span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">m1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">m1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span><font color=\"#000000\">NA</font></span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)*</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">rskminor</span><br></div></code></div><div>But that doesn&#39;t work.</div></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div>That is not the way to use NAs.  NAs (for &quot;free this parameter&quot;) are only to be mixed with fixed values, such as  </div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#606\">Deter</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">NA</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NA</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rskminor</span></div></code></div><br></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div><br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div> The final solution was to assign a specific label to each parameter I want to estimate</div></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Deter</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=~</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> c</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">m2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">m1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">m1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">m3</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)*</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">rskminor</span></div></code></div></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div>This is the correct way to set equality constraints on a subset of freely estimated parameters.</div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div><br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Maybe an equal example could be added to the tutorial? </div></div></blockquote><div><br></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div><a href=\"http://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/groups.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/groups.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792425761856000&amp;usg=AOvVaw023HmDc_03drsK406Zqhkf\">http://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/groups.html</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>See sections in the second half of the page: &quot;<b>Fixing parameters in some groups, but not all</b>&quot; and &quot;<b>Constraining a single parameter to be equal across groups</b>&quot;.</div>"
    ],
